== en
titulo: Free time
intro: Learn how to talk about hobbies and leisure activities, distinguishing between jugar and tocar.
b1.titulo: Jugar versus tocar
b1.texto: "Spanish uses two different verbs where English uses *play*:\n\n- For sports and games, use **jugar a** + article: **juego al fútbol**, **al tenis**, **a las cartas** (*a + el = al*).\n- For musical instruments, use **tocar** + article: **toco la guitarra**, **el piano**.\n\nThe verb **jugar** has a stem change (u → ue) in stressed forms: *juego, juegas, juega, juegan* (but *jugamos, jugáis*).\n\nOther common leisure activities: **hacer deporte**, **ver la tele**, **escuchar música**, **leer**, **nadar**, **pasear**, **ir de compras**, **viajar**."
b2.titulo: What do you do in your free time?
b3.titulo: Leisure and hobby vocabulary
b4.titulo: Using tocar and jugar
b4.texto: Compare playing an instrument with playing a sport or game.
b5.titulo: Shared hobbies
b6.titulo: Leisure verbs question
b6.pregunta: How do you say playing a musical instrument in Spanish?
b6.o0.refuerzo: Exactly! Musical instruments always take tocar.
b6.o1.refuerzo: Jugar is used for sports and games, never instruments.
b6.o2.refuerzo: Hacer is not used with instruments.
b7.titulo: Complete with preposition and article
b7.pregunta: Choose the contracted form to play a sport.
b7.o0.refuerzo: Correct! Jugar a + el tenis contracts to al tenis.
b7.o1.refuerzo: The mandatory preposition a is missing.
b7.o2.refuerzo: Tenis is a masculine noun.
b8.titulo: Order the words
b8.traduccion: I play tennis on Saturdays.
b9.titulo: Write the translation
b9.pregunta: Translate into Spanish: «I like reading.»
p.el tiempo libre.glosa: free time
p.el tiempo libre.consejo: Leisure or spare time.
